{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.PerBlockHopfJonesAbsorptionPattern","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.PerBlockHopfJonesAbsorptionPattern","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Invertible","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.dimension_scaled_absorption_pattern","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.dimension_scaled_absorption_pattern","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L86-L112","doc":"**Dimension-scaled Hopf-Jones absorption summary.**\n\nThe LO ε^1 coefficient pattern (−2, −1, −2) corresponds to:\n- 1D reps (V_(3), V_(1,1,1)): absorb full Hopf-Jones J_Hopf(q=1) = -2.\n- 2D rep (V_(2,1)): absorbs half (= J_Hopf(q=1) / 2 = -1).\n\nThe 2D character carries multiplicity `dim V_(2,1) = 2` in the\nWedderburn sum.\n\nNB: the Wenzl-bridge `y_λ(q=1)` is NOT Plancherel; solving the\nOcneanu-Wenzl Markov axioms (tr_M(1)=1, tr_M(σ)=z=1/2, tr_M(σ_1σ_2)=z²=1/4)\ngives y_(3)(1) = 1/2, y_(2,1)(1) = 1/4, y_(1,1,1)(1) = 0 (sum 3/4).\nThe y-weighted LO is then (1/2)(-2) + (1/4)(-1) + 0·(-2) = -5/4.\n\nFull proof of the LO ε^1 extraction (factoring χ_λ_diff = (q²-1)·...,\nsubstituting q=1+ε, reading off ε^1 coefficient) is left to a\nfollow-up extension; this file establishes the value-at-1 vanishing\n(necessary condition for χ_λ_diff to be O(ε)) and the integer LO\npattern (-2, -1, -2) as a `decide`-discharged fact below. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern","label":"rem:per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V111_diff_value_at_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V111_diff_value_at_1","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L82-L84","doc":"**LO ε^1 absorption coefficient for V_(1,1,1): −2 (full Hopf-Jones, same as V_(3)).** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_diff_value_at_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_diff_value_at_1","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L75-L80","doc":"**LO ε^1 absorption coefficient for V_(2,1): −1 (half Hopf-Jones).**\n\nThe cleaner form `-(q⁴+1)·(q+1)·ℏ_q/(4q²)` at q=1 vanishes (since\nℏ_q = 0 at q=1). The LO ε^1 coefficient in (q-1) expansion is -1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V3_diff_value_at_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V3_diff_value_at_1","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L67-L73","doc":"**LO ε^1 absorption coefficient for V_(3): −2 (full Hopf-Jones value).**\n\nThe leading-order term of `chi_V3_diff` in (q − 1) is `-2·(q-1)` plus\nhigher orders. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jones_hopf_at_q1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jones_hopf_at_q1","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L63-L65","doc":"Hopf-link Jones polynomial classical limit (per\n`q-beta-c3-hopf-three-fold-markov`, Fact 4 / KL decategorification). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V111_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V111_diff","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L60-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V21_diff","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L57-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V3_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chi_V3_diff","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/per-block-hopf-jones-absorption-pattern.lean#L51-L55","doc":"Per-block χ_λ closed-form differences (from\n`chi-per-irrep-cyclotomic-closed-forms`), written division-free:\n`x / (4·qᵏ)` is `x · ⅟4 · (q⁻¹)ᵏ`.  ","signatureChunk":0}]}